# Cartique Ecommerce Module - Technical Brief

## Overview
Cartique is a standalone, vanilla JavaScript ecommerce frontend module designed for product catalog display, shopping cart management, and checkout functionality. It's built to be framework-agnostic and can be integrated into any web project with minimal configuration.

## Architecture

### Core Structure

```
Cartique/
├── Core Engine
│   ├── Configuration & Feature Management
│   ├── Data State Management
│   ├── Filtering & Search Logic
│   └── Event System
├── Rendering Components
│   ├── Product Grid/List Views
│   ├── Single Product View
│   ├── Shopping Cart (Slide-in & Full Page)
│   ├── Sidebar Filters
│   ├── Category Menu
│   └── Search & Sort Controls
└── Integration Layer
    ├── LocalStorage Cart Persistence
    ├── Callback System
    └── External Service Hooks
```

### Key Components

#### 1. **Product Display System**
- **Dual Layout Support**: Grid and list views with seamless switching
- **Infinite Scroll**: Batch loading with intersection observer
- **Single Product View**: Detailed product view with tabs for details and reviews
- **Stock Management**: Real-time inventory display and validation

#### 2. **Filtering & Search Engine**
- **Multi-dimensional Filtering**: Category, price range, and variant attributes
- **Real-time Search**: Debounced search across product titles and descriptions
- **Category Navigation**: Mega menu and sidebar category filters with sync
- **Sorting**: Multiple sort options (price, title, relevance)

#### 3. **Shopping Cart System**
- **Dual Interface**: Slide-in cart for quick access and full-page cart view
- **Quantity Management**: Increment/decrement with stock validation
- **Persistence**: LocalStorage-based cart persistence
- **Real-time Updates**: Subtotal calculation and cart count updates

#### 4. **Review & Rating System**
- **Rating Display**: Star ratings with distribution visualization
- **Review Submission**: Form-based review input with callback support
- **Customer Attribution**: Support for logged-in and guest users

